{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"execute_python","description":"Execute ordinary persistent Python with stdout/stderr over CAPTURE_REPLAY inputs. geometry={'objects':[{'name':str,'vertices':[[rational_x,rational_y,rational_z],...],'triangles':[[i,j,k],...]}]} and cameras={'views':[{'name':str,'view_matrix':4x4,'projection_matrix':4x4,'direction_rational':[x,y,z],'size_px':[512,512],...}],...} reside in Python. np and Fraction are available. Raw inputs are returned only when requested or printed. render_views(names,include_images=False) batch-renders current frozen inputs and returns refs/buffer handles. Every requested view is a fresh actual construction, including repeats. buffers[view] contains color uint8[H,W,3], depth float64[H,W], owners int32[H,W] and triangle_ids int32[H,W]. Pixel origin is top-left, indices zero-based. owners identifies geometry.objects; triangle_ids is the global source-face index in object/face input order. Both owners use -1 for background; background depth is infinity. Base material RGB is (180,190,205). rendered RGB retains the common geometry-based shading. Merge source triangle IDs into your own target surface before boundary/readability calculations. Count unique target-owned pixels incident to horizontal/vertical different-surface pairs with RGB distance at least 24, marking both endpoints. read_images(refs) or attach_images(refs) appends actual generated images to this result; render_views(...,include_images=True) combines generation and image delivery. Existing buffers and image refs can be reused directly. scratch is a writable Path, image_files maps refs to generated PNG paths. Use ordinary Python/NumPy/Fraction and your own algorithms. Product discovery, visibility-index, selection and location aggregation APIs are outside this common tool. Keep source inputs unchanged.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"scene_data","description":"Read complete raw CAPTURE_REPLAY world geometry and candidate camera parameters. The same objects are already in execute_python variables geometry and cameras.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"render_views","description":"Generate one or multiple full-scene views using the shared exact inputs and common RGB/depth/owner renderer. Return stable current-session refs and raw buffer handles. Every requested view constructs a fresh frame, including repeats. Existing buffers and refs can be read again. include_images requests actual image content in this result.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"names":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["SCENE","TOP","LEFT","RIGHT","FRONT","BACK"]}},"include_images":{"type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["names"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"read_images","description":"Return actual 512x512 PNG image content for one or multiple generated current-session image refs. Input order is retained. The source views reuse their render cache.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"refs":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["refs"],"additionalProperties":false}}]}}
